recommendation:
Call updateFeeCredit before resetting the offset:

function onBalanceChange(address token, address account) public onlyManager {
    updateFeeCredit(token, account); // credit pending fees first
    if (balanceOf(token, account) > 0) {
        if (userTokens[account].length == 0 || /* not already tracked */) {
            userTokens[account].push(token);
        }
    }
}

Use .call{value:} instead of .transfer():

(bool success, ) = payable(msg.sender).call{value: claimable}("");
require(success, "ETH transfer failed");

Also apply checks-effects-interactions: set unclaimedFees to 0 before the external call (already done in the current code, which is correct).

Use `require()` or custom errors in both modifiers:


modifier onlyOwner() {
    require(msg.sender == owner, 'Not owner');
    _;
}

modifier onlyManager() {
    require(managers[msg.sender], 'Not manager');
    _;
}

Or with custom errors (more gas efficient):

error NotOwner();
error NotManager();

modifier onlyOwner() {
    if (msg.sender != owner) revert NotOwner();
    _;
}

modifier onlyManager() {
    if (!managers[msg.sender]) revert NotManager();
    _;
}

Update the `transferOwnership` function to also update the managers mapping:


function transferOwnership(address owner_) public onlyOwner {
    require(owner_ != address(0), 'New owner is zero address');
    managers[owner] = false;  // Remove old owner from managers
    owner = owner_;
    managers[owner_] = true;  // Add new owner as manager
}
